d Log Drains issue and we are rolling out a fix. Oct 21 , 00:56 UTC Update - We are investigating errors affecting runtime Logs and Log Drains. Oct 21 , 00:32 UTC Update - Edge Config issues are now resolved. Oct 21 , 00:08 UTC Update - Domain Registrations issues are now resolved. Oct 20 , 23:14 UTC Update - A fix has been implemented for Edge Config, and we are monitoring the result. Oct 20 , 21:57 UTC Update - A fix has been implemented for Domain Registrations, and we are monitoring the result. Oct 20 , 21:50 UTC Update - We have identified Domain Registration failures and are working to restore service. Oct 20 , 21:34 UTC Update - We have identified degraded performance with Edge Config storage and are working to restore service. Oct 20 , 20:24 UTC Update - New deployments using Routing Middleware or Vercel Functions in the IAD1 region may fail to deploy. Traffic is still successfully being rerouted away from IAD1, which may result in increased latency. We are seeing full recovery of Edge Function and Middleware invocation errors in our IAD1 region. We are investigating an intermittent elevation of Cron Jobs not being executed. Historical data for Speed Insights and Web Analytics is currently being backfilled. Oct 20 , 18:45 UTC Update - New deployments using Routing Middleware or Vercel Functions in the IAD1 region may fail to deploy. Traffic is still successfully being rerouted away from IAD1, which may result in increased latency. We are seeing full recovery of Edge Function and Middleware invocation errors in our IAD1 region. We are investigating an intermittent elevation of Cron Jobs not being executed. Historical data for Speed Insights and Web Analytics is currently being backfilled. Oct 20 , 18:40 UTC Update - We are seeing recovery across Edge Functions and Middleware invocation errors in our IAD1 region. Historical data for Speed Insights and Web Analytics is currently being backfilled. Deployment creation for customers using Secure Compute or Static IPs are still impacted. Traffic is still successfully being rerouted away from iad1, which may result in increased latency. Oct 20 , 18:06 UTC Update - We are investigating an intermittent elevation of Edge Function and Middleware invocation errors in our IAD1 region. Impacted customers may encounter errors with the code INTERNAL_FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED. Historical data for Speed Insights and Web Analytics is currently being backfilled. Deployment creation for customers using Secure Compute or Static IPs are still impacted. Traffic is still successfully being rerouted away from iad1, which may result in increased latency. Oct 20 , 17:36 UTC Update - Historical data for Speed Insights and Web Analytics is currently being backfilled. Deployment creation for customers not using Secure Compute or Static IPs has been fully restored. Traffic is still successfully being rerouted away from IAD1, which may result in increased latency. Oct 20 , 16:12 UTC Update - We are currently investigating reports of delayed data for Speed Insights and Web Analytics. Oct 20 , 15:38 UTC Update - We are currently investigating reports of delayed data for Speed Insights and Web Analytics. Oct 20 , 15:32 UTC Update - We are seeing recovery across deployment creation using Routing Middleware and Functions in IAD1. CDN traffic in IAD1 continues to be rerouted as we work toward full recovery. During this period, users may experience increased latency. Oct 20 , 12:17 UTC Update - We are continuing to work on a fix for this issue. Oct 20 , 10:28 UTC Update - We are continuing to work on a fix for this issue. Oct 20 , 10:27 UTC Update - New deployments using Routing Middleware, or Vercel Functions with iad1 region may still be failing. We are continuing to investigate this issue. Oct 20 , 10:16 UTC Update - We are seeing recovery across services and CDN traffic is healthy. Oct 20 , 08:45 UTC Identified - Multiple services are affected. We have re-routed CDN traffic from iad1 to a healthy region and are working on managing impact by component. Builds have also been rerouted. Oct 20 , 08:03 UTC Update - We are continuing to investigate this issue. Oct 20 , 07:50 UTC Update - We are continuing to investigate this issue. Oct 20 , 07:40 UTC Update - We are continuing to investigate this issue. Oct 20 , 07:33 UTC Update - We are continuing to investigate this issue. Oct 20 , 07:33 UTC Investigating - We are currently investigating this issue. Oct 20 , 07:30 UTC Major outage on API, Dashboard, and Builds Resolved - This incident has been resolved. Oct 21 , 00:04 UTC Monitoring - The Vercel API has now been fully resolved. We are continuing to monitor the Dashboard performance. Oct 20 , 23:50 UTC Update - Builds are now being created as expected and are fully resolved. Oct 20 , 23:27 UTC Update - We continue to work on resolving the Dashboard and API failures. Oct 20 , 22:20 UTC Update - We have processed a backlog of builds but we are still observing errors initiating new builds. We have determined the root cause and are working on a fix. Oct 20 , 22:08 UTC Update - We have identified the root cause of build failures and are working on a fix. Oct 20 , 21:52 UTC Identified - We have identified the root cause of the Dashboard degradation, and a fix is being worked on. Oct 20 , 21:12 UTC Investigating - Increased Vercel dashboard failures, API failures, and deployment failures. CDN requests are functioning as expected. Oct 20 , 20:00 UTC Oct 20 , 2025 Oct 19 , 2025 No incidents reported. Oct 18 , 2025 No incidents reported. Oct 17 , 2025 No incidents reported. Oct 16 , 2025 Domain details for domains owned by account scopes can&amp;apos;t be accessed Resolved - This incident has been resolved. Oct 16 , 09:20 UTC Monitoring - A fix has been implemented and we are monitoring the results. Oct 16 , 08:50 UTC Identified - The issue has been identified and a fix is being implemented. Oct 16 , 08:38 UTC Update - We are continuing to investigate this issue. Oct 16 , 07:09 UTC Investigating - Details for domains belonging to account scopes ( https://vercel.com/account/domains ) return 404. If changes need to be made, we recommend transferring these domains to a team scope from this dashboard. Oct 16 , 05:25 UTC Oct 15 , 2025 No incidents reported. Oct 14 , 2025 No incidents reported. Oct 13 , 2025 No incidents reported. Oct 12 , 2025 No incidents reported. Oct 11 , 2025 No incidents reported. Oct 10 , 2025 AI SDK and Next.js Learn are unable to sign in to Vercel Resolved - The incident has been resolved, and sign in is possible again. Oct 10 , 03:10 UTC Identified - The issue has been identified, and a fix is being implemented. Oct 10 , 02:44 UTC Investigating - Weundefinedre currently investigating an issue where https://ai-sdk.dev/ and https://nextjs.org/learn/dashboard-app are unable to sign in with Vercel. Oct 10 , 02:37 UTC Oct 9 , 2025 No incidents reported. &amp;larr; Incident History Powered by Atlassian Statuspage</code></pre>
